<title>ITALY: Italian cabinet approves mini-budget.</title>
<headline>Italian cabinet approves mini-budget.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian cabinet on Thursday approved a corrective budget needed to keep the country on track to enter the single European currency.</p>
<p>Prime Minister Romano Prodi told reporters the mini-budget would include 15.5 trillion lire ($9.2 billion) of deficit cuts needed to plug a hole in Italy's state accounts and meet the terms of the Maastricht Treaty. ($ = 1677 Italian Lire)</p>
</text>
